Package: stablr
Title: Kinetic Modeling of Pharmaceutical Stability Data
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Federico", family = "Ferrari", email = "federico.ferrari@msd.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(given = "Samantha", family = "Gleich", email = "samantha.gleich@msd.com", role = c("aut")),
    person(given = "Michael", family = "Johnson", email = "michael.johnson6@msd.com", role = c("aut")),
    person(given = "Qiaohui", family = "Zhou", email = "qiaohui.zhou@msd.com", role = c("aut"))
    )
Description: Fits kinetic models to pharmaceutical stability data using
    nonlinear least squares. Supported models include the Sestak-Berggren
    solid-state degradation model solved as an ordinary differential
    equation, single-step degradation, and parallel degradation into two
    products. Temperature and relative humidity dependence of reaction rates
    is described with the Arrhenius and humidity-modified Arrhenius
    equations. Provides confidence, prediction and tolerance intervals for
    model predictions, predictions under time-varying temperature profiles,
    and simulation of stability data.
